miyoo button codes

The hall sensor needs a lid cycle before it tells the truth. It reads 0 --
closed -- from boot until the lid is actually opened once, whatever the lid is
really doing, so slot's first poll believed the lid was shut on every boot,
dozed, and left the handheld starting to a black screen that a POWER press
woke. Reported as "still black on boot" and found by sampling hallvalue and
the PWM duty together across a real lid cycle: 26 seconds of hallvalue=0 with
the lid open and the panel lit, then correct readings for every cycle after.

So nothing is believed until the sensor says open once. The cost is that the
first close after a boot is not slot's to act on -- the kernel suspends a
moment later and blanks the panel itself, which is what happens for that one
cycle anyway -- and `lid_event` is pulled out of the poll so both halves can
be tested without a device.

